{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear ~4% improvement over the rna_only baseline (config_001, 0.485 acc). This confirms that adding a ResNet50 image branch with concat fusion is beneficial. However, all experiments so far use singleprofile; the multiprofile axis is entirely untested and represents the largest remaining source of uncertainty about whether additional per-cell profile information can further boost performance. Question tested: Does switching from singleprofile to multiprofile (with avgpool aggregation) improve on the validated multimodal+concat setup, while keeping RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat) identical to config_016? This isolates the profile-setting effect. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the minimal, cleanest extension of our best-performing configuration along the most impactful untested design axis. A positive result would justify investing further in multiprofile variants (transformer aggregation, other encoders); a null or negative result would let us redirect budget toward RNA/image encoder choices and fusion strategy, avoiding wasted experiments on a less productive axis. Under a tight budget, resolving this binary question about multiprofile value is more informative than, e.g., testing weighted vs. concat fusion on singleprofile, where the expected delta is smaller."
}

